WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.352
Welcome to Module 12, Cleaning and Exploratory Data Analysis.

00:00:05.352 --> 00:00:10.152
In the previous module, we learned how to build more advanced Pandas workflows.

00:00:10.152 --> 00:00:17.197
Now we are going to use those tools for one of the most important parts of analytics:

00:00:17.197 --> 00:00:21.442
deciding whether the data is trustworthy enough to analyze.

00:00:21.442 --> 00:00:25.652
Cleaning is not simply deleting rows that look unusual.

00:00:25.652 --> 00:00:31.722
It means understanding the quality of the data, correcting problems when we have a good reason,

00:00:31.722 --> 00:00:33.914
and documenting what we changed.

00:00:34.491 --> 00:00:39.622
After cleaning, we move into exploratory data analysis, or EDA.

00:00:39.622 --> 00:00:45.503
EDA helps us understand what is in the dataset before we make stronger conclusions.

00:00:45.503 --> 00:00:54.912
We look at missing values, duplicate records, data types, categories, unusual values, and basic patterns.

00:00:54.912 --> 00:00:59.342
Throughout this module, keep asking two questions: what problem do I see in the data,

00:00:59.342 --> 00:01:05.350
and what evidence supports the cleaning decision I am making?
